  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\n\nThe H5 wave and vort max will traverse the state on Monday. Expect \ncontinued rain chances for portions of northeast Nebraska (60-80% \nchance). Some deterministic and ensemble guidance suggests the \nprecip may overspread the rest of eastern Nebraska, but chances \nremain at 15% or less.\n\nSfc high pressure moves in behind the departing wave for Tuesday, \nbut another mid level wave approaches the area from eastern Kansas. \nSouthwesterly flow and some lift aided by H8 WAA may generate some \nmore scattered showers along the Kansas/Nebraska border, but chances \nagain remain less than 25%. \n\nContinued zonal to southwesterly flow will allow several H5 waves to \ntraverse the flow and lead to more periodic chances for rain showers \n(15-30% chance Wednesday through Friday). Late in the period, \nthere is some indication amongst model guidance for a deepening \nlongwave across the western CONUS. As the wave approaches the \narea, should see more rain chances overspread the area by late \nFriday (50-60%).\n\nTemperatures during this period will largely remain in the upper 50s \nand 60s for most areas. 70s return for most areas after Wednesday.",
